1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,018
Chapter 7. Everyone plays.

2
00:00:03,318 --> 00:00:15,770
In 2006, the Wii did the unthinkable: it got people playing who had never touched a controller. Grandparents. Parents. Kids. Everyone swinging their arm in front of the TV.

3
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:18,969
Over 101 million consoles.

4
00:00:19,149 --> 00:00:27,225
Then came smartphones. Today, more than half of the industry's revenue comes from a screen we carry in our pocket.

5
00:00:27,405 --> 00:00:38,876
In 2011, a game made of blocks left beta behind. Minecraft. Over 350 million copies: the best-selling game in history.

6
00:00:39,056 --> 00:00:45,019
And on September 17, 2013, that name returned. GTA V.

7
00:00:45,569 --> 00:00:55,380
In three days it grossed $1 billion. No movie, no album, no entertainment product had ever done it that fast.
